            name = f.attr if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) else (f.id if isinstance(f, ast.Name) else None)\n            if name in HELPERS and n.args and names_root(n.args[0]):\n                hits.append((name, n.lineno))\n    if hits:\n        print(p.name, hits)\nPY\npython3 /tmp/probe_scan.py","description":"Prototype widened scan"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QJ9WHD4P9YutQsdyZYn7RY","tool_input":{"command":"rm -f probe_scan.py; time .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q 2>&1 | tail -40","timeout":900000,"description":"Full suite with timing"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The suite is green. Here is what landed and — importantly — what did not.\n\n## Delivered\n\n**Builder and materializer (`tests/conftest.py`).** `build_workflow(*stages, name=..., escalation_rules=...)` with `workflow_stage(...)` and `StageRef(index)` for routes. Every key not asked for is absent, so a test can build a case this repository does not deploy. `materialize_workflow(workflow, root, ...)` writes the definition, a prompt per stage, and links rules/schemas — and `copy=(\"orchestration\",\"scripts\")` for a run driven through an entry point (`resolve()` would otherwise follow a symlink back here). A `configured_workflow` fixture seam lets `target_root` drive a built definition.\n\n**Widened scan (`tests/test_baseline_honesty.py`).** A second route matching `shipped_workflow`/`load_workflow` against a repository-root argument *or an omitted one* (both default to this repository). Controls: five planted helper-route spellings each reported; a builder-only module not reported; and `build_workflow` shown to open no file by instrumenting `Path.open`/`Path.read_text` rather than by scanning its source. The stated limits were rewritten and re-asserted — the helper limit narrowed rather than disappeared.\n\n**Declared list.** `GRANDFATHERED_LIVE_ARTIFACT_READERS` → `PERMITTED_LIVE_ARTIFACT_READERS`, a dict of 30 modules each carrying a stated reason, asserted equal to the scan's report in both directions, written out rather than derived, with no two reasons alike.\n\n**`tests/test_shipped_workflow_is_valid.py`** (21 tests). The shipped definition against `self_route_problems`, `retry_routing_problems`, `stage_exception_problems`, each paired with a built definition that violates it. Plus the displaced configuration assertions and the demonstration that a deployment change moves this module.\n\n**Runtime:** before 474.49 s (7:54, 2449 tests) → after **441.92 s (7:21, 2479 tests)**. Both measured, same machine, `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`.\n\n## Not delivered\n\n**Only one module was converted** — `tests/test_story_coordinator.py`, which now builds its own four-stage workflow, materializes it, and is off the scan's report. The story's list of ~20 input readers, including the two its own plan names first (`test_self_routing_retry.py`, `test_retry_routing.py`), is untouched. Those modules stay on the declared list, and their reasons describe the shipped reads that remain (schemas, rules, prompts) rather than claiming their workflow read was classified as a subject. That is an honest list, but it is not the reduced list the story asked for, and criteria about converted assertions still biting and about displaced assertions from those modules are correspondingly unmet.\n\nOne existing assertion needed repair: `test_git_history_loading_retired.py` scanned conftest for a bare `\"clean_clone\"` to catch a frozen workflow copy; the builder's kwarg tripped it. Narrowed to the mapping-literal form `'\"clean_clone\": '`, with a control constructing the frozen form beside it.","ttft_ms":2612,"ttft_stream_ms":1162,"time_to_request_ms":20,"type":"result","duration_ms":2047506,"uuid":"820c20f0-5a67-472a-a123-8df40de4fe4e"}
