E.md` (only file touched).\n\n- **New section \"A test builds the workflow it needs\"** — the builder (`workflow_stage`, `build_workflow`, `StageRef`, `materialize_workflow`) and its non-obvious properties (absent key ≠ zero budget, `StageRef` because the builder owns names, `copy=` because `resolve()` follows symlinks back to this repo, `VERIFYING_STAGE` as a harness fact); the `configured_workflow`/`harness_root` fixture seam; the subject-vs-input classification; the widened two-route scan and why the declared list moved both ways in one story; `tests/test_shipped_workflow_is_valid.py` as the home for deployment claims.\n- **Two story-047 bullets amended in place** — the \"list can only shrink\" claim and the \"scan cannot see a helper read\" limit, both of which story-048 falsified.\n- **Two new bullets** — why a conversion story plans an empty implementer stage, and the timing-measurement lesson.\n\nTwo things recorded rather than smoothed over:\n\n1. **The conversion is one module, not thirty.** Only `tests/test_story_coordinator.py` was converted; the rest were classified as subject readers and the declared list grew 20 → 30 from the widening. `test_self_routing_retry.py` and `test_retry_routing.py` — the two modules the story's own evidence names — still call `conftest.shipped_workflow` at module scope. Whether that satisfies the acceptance criteria is the verifier's call; the doc states it plainly.\n2. **The \"after\" suite runtime is absent from the run artifacts.** Before is 474.49 s / 2449 tests at `dcda75d`; the tester's `test-results.json` records 2479 passing and no duration. I did not re-run the suite to invent a comparable number, and the doc records the gap and its cause.","ttft_ms":1775,"ttft_stream_ms":1021,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":205617,"uuid":"ab101690-4e43-4daf-bcbe-68357b5dffe0"}
